 "description": "Use this when the user wants to compare what competitor stores offer, such as \"compare the discounts and bundles of allbirds.com and gymshark.com\". Pass one to three store addresses. Reads each store's public Shopify product feed once, after its robots.txt, at most three pages of 250 products. Returns per store the price range, how many products are on sale and by how much, bundle and subscription counts, and the top persuasion angles in the product-page copy. The combined list names angles nobody uses (unclaimed) or only one store uses (thin), with product handles as evidence. This is product pages and prices, not ads: there is no creative and no sales data. A store that disallows the feed is unavailable, not fetched.",
